{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795356674,"nonce":"YGKtLvqlz2H8/pz8XynlR32OX+M=","title":"A value array's element data is not 16-byte aligned, so vector loops over hl.NativeArray run about 2x slower than over hl.Bytes","message":"Reported by the hxn session. The same Single integration loop (vel += g*dt; pos += vel*dt over 4096 elements, both arrays held as object fields, 4000 passes) runs at 0.22 ns per element over hl.NativeArray\u003cSingle\u003e and 0.10 over hl.Bytes, in hybrid, jit and llvm-tier modes. Reproducer: NaGap.hx from the hxn session (build with `haxe -main NaGap -hl nagap.hl`).\n\nCause. The LLVM bodies for the two loops are the same vectorized code (4 x float, interleave 2, runtime alias check). The only difference is the data address. A varray header is 24 bytes, the allocator returns 16-byte aligned blocks, so NativeArray data sits at 8 mod 16 and every 16-byte vector access straddles a 16-byte boundary.\n\nConfirmed by running the Bytes loop at controlled byte offsets from a 64-byte boundary: offsets 0 and 16 run at 0.10 ns per element; offsets 4, 8, 12, 24, 40 and 56 all run at 0.22. Any data address that is not 16-byte aligned pays.\n\nFix. hlp_alloc_array starts a value array (no heap pointers) with at least 16 bytes of element data 8 bytes into its allocation, so the data lands on a 16-byte boundary. Cost is nothing when the data size is a multiple of 16 and 16 bytes otherwise. Pointer arrays are scanned and stay at the allocation start. The collector resolves interior pointers to their allocation through containing_allocation and nothing moves objects.\n\nResult on the Mac, release build, same reproducer: hybrid 0.215 -\u003e 0.104 (Bytes 0.107), jit 0.219 -\u003e 0.107 (Bytes 0.105), llvm tier 0.259 -\u003e 0.142 (Bytes 0.133, noisy). Linux not yet measured.\n\nNot covered: hl.Bytes values that a program offsets by a non-multiple of 16 (hl.Bytes.offset), and arrays from HDLLs that allocate their own memory.","files":null}]}